<title>SPAIN: Popular to cancel 4.5 pct of shares, cut nominal.</title>
<headline>Popular to cancel 4.5 pct of shares, cut nominal.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Popular will buy back back up to 35 billion pesetas' worth of shares to a limit of 4.5 percent of share capital, to be cancelled in June, the bank's technical director Manuel Martin said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bank also agreed a one to four share split, with the share nominal falling to 125 pesetas from 500 pesetas at present, Martin told journalists.</p>
</text>
